Pyro patch 0038: inline module scripts resolve against a base URL the embedder registers.

An inline module script needs a registry identity of its own (JSC evaluates a key once), but its
specifiers resolve against its base URL: the document base URL when it was prepared, fragment and
all. Patch 0005 had the embedder key it `<document URL>#inline-module-N` and dropped the whole
fragment of any referrer containing that text before matching import map scopes, which also cut the
authored fragment of an inline script's base and of a fetched module whose URL merely contained the
text, and let a fetched module named like an inline identity collide with it.
JSGlobalContextSetInlineModuleBase (JSModuleLoaderRefPrivate.h) associates an identity with its base
URL. resolveModuleSpecifier resolves a registered referrer against that base (scopes match it as
given) and keeps the identity itself when it is loaded as an entry point, so it need not be a URL;
the text-marker fragment removal is gone. The identity's source carries the base URL (its stack
frames and dynamic import() referrer), which the fetch resolution accepts for that identity instead
of requiring the source URL to equal the key.

